<classification-symbol scheme="ICO">M03C214:30</classification-symbol><classification-symbol scheme="ICO">T01F17:00A2</classification-symbol><classification-symbol scheme="ICO">T05K1:03B</classification-symbol></classification-ecla><invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="EN">GLASS CERAMICS COMPOSITION AND ELECTRONIC PARTS AND MULTILAYERED LC MULTIPLE COMPONENT USING THE SAME</invention-title><invention-title load-source="docdb"  status="new" lang="FR">COMPOSITION VERRE-CERAMIQUE, COMPOSANTS ELECTRONIQUES ET MULTICOMPOSANT LC MULTICOUCHE UTILISANT LADITE COMPOSITION</invention-title><citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-10106880-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>10106880</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations> <non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1130003A1</text><sources><source name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations> </technical-data> <parties><applicants><applicant status="new"  format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAKA MASAHIRO</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATSUMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC IND CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSUMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAKA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATSUMURA HIDENORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAITO RYUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAKA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSUMURA, HIDENORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAITO, RYUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A maltilayered LC multiple component being composed of a glass ceramics composition, which is excellent in packaging reliability especially in relation to a resin substrate and in electric properties at a high frequency and can be produced with ease, and internal electrodes containing silver or copper as a main component.  The glass ceramics composition comprises 45 to 35 wt % of a forsterite powder and 55 to 65 wt % of a glass powder, wherein the glass powder comprises 40 to 50 wt % of SiO2, 30 to 40 wt % of BaO, 3 to 8 wt % of Al2O3, 8 to 12 wt % of La2O3 and 3 to 6 wt % of B2O3.  It has a high bending strength and an appropriately high thermal expansion coefficient and can easily form a green sheet, and also can be sintered tightly at a temperature less than 950  DEG C.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un multicomposant LC multicouche constitué d'une part, d'une composition verre-céramique, excellente du point de vue de la fiabilité de l'emballage, notamment pour un substrat de résine, et de ses propriétés électriques à fréquence élevée, et qui peut être produite facilement, et d'autre part, d'électrodes internes contenant comme composant principal de l'argent ou du cuivre. La composition vitrocéramique renferme de 45 à 35 % en poids d'une poudre de forstérite et de 55 à 65 % en poids d'une poudre de verre, la poudre de verre comprenant de 40 à 50 % en poids de SiO2, de 30 à 40 % en poids de BaO, de 3 à 8 % en poids de Al2O3, de 8 à 12 % en poids de La2O3, et de 3 à 6 % en poids de B2O3. Le composant selon l'invention possède une résistance à la flexion élevée et un coefficient de dilatation thermique suffisamment élevé ; il peut facilement former une feuille crue, et peut être fritté de façon très compacte à une température inférieure à 950  DEG C.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>